entries.english:
Heinrich von Rossach and his wife Agnes sell the following properties in Oberlauringen to Wilhelm von Schaumberg zu Thundorf:
- One-sixth of the tithe;
- the right to redeem half a dwelling and yard, which had previously belonged to their cousin Vinzenz von Rossach;
- all their allodial properties and the fiefs they hold there from the Bishopric of Würzburg;
- three storehouses in the churchyard;
- and the mill below the village.
The buyer has paid them 1,100 Rhenish gulden for these. They therefore transfer to him the sold rights and properties with all rights belonging to them therein, and warrant the sale.
Seals: Heinrich von Rossach for himself and his wife (1), and, at their request, Ciriacus von Maßbach (2).

Notes: Abstracts (15th and 17th centuries).
